## 5. REPRO-FIRST DEBUGGING
When debugging unexpected behavior or fixing bugs:
1. First, create a minimal isolated reproduction script or unit test to prove the bug exists.
2. Run the test and confirm it fails.
3. Apply the targeted fix.
4. Re-run the test and confirm it passes.
5. Clean up temporary reproduction artifacts before finishing the task.

